entView","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The complement: the same vertices, and an edge u→v for every ordered pair of distinct"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices that the graph does not join (NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"complement"},{"type":"text","text":", igraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"complementer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loops=False"},{"type":"text","text":"). Self-loops and parallel edges of the graph are ignored, so the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"complement is simple and loop-free, and the complement of the complement is the graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"made simple and loop-free. O(1); a lazy view."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/complementview","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"complementView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ComplementView","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:15GraphOperations14ComplementViewV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol"}}}